    "text": "firstalert4.com\nwebsite\nJefferson County, Missouri\nJefferson County inches closer to banning swimming at Rockford Park\nBy First Alert 4 StaffCameron Bopp,\n1 days agoJEFFERSON COUNTY, Mo. (First Alert 4) - Jefferson County leaders are moving forward with a proposal to ban swimming at Rockford Park. The park, located along the Big River just off Highway 30 near Byrnes Mill, has been the site of repeated emergencies. In the last decade, officials say there have been dozens of emergency calls and at least seven drownings, despite signs warning people to swim at their own risk.\n3",
